#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f04b25d-f38d-5fc1-9876-423c80368bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242439} {:answer/id #uuid "b15931fb-52e5-5c41-a258-369e7d1fb1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242724} {:answer/id #uuid "b42567a6-9890-5794-8a22-d6d56c1dc629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242754} {:answer/id #uuid "d0121691-eca2-5974-80e3-dbeade97f6d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243013} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e06cb0-4838-5459-9758-b2749164bf96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15931fb-52e5-5c41-a258-369e7d1fb1c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242724} :answer-field/id #uuid "e685e6a5-808d-5d60-91f6-26ddb332e292" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5dfc56d2-f4d4-58d9-9174-ebcc9a95025f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106781" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=6+2t.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(1-t+2{t}^{2}) & =6+2t \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =6+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$  Substituting this into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+(-2)=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ad0a48-81fc-5240-8a93-2ba2c02e3c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357943} {:answer/id #uuid "298460b6-9c2f-56b8-8ced-e7d6ae2bf14d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358131} {:answer/id #uuid "506aad2b-31aa-5dd1-9a29-689248019180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358442} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf66e93-e3a6-5ef3-b5de-a6b3e747467b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359407} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b3d49c-e9eb-52f4-b6f4-05e5551e3f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdf66e93-e3a6-5ef3-b5de-a6b3e747467b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359407} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b78b52-cccd-55ae-b45f-93187dd919d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3294d22f-a9c0-5f7d-ab23-cc174247e4c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95021" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & -3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 9{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -6{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d93c2e02-a22d-58cb-9c87-b91a9cb4dfcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366589} {:answer/id #uuid "10929a25-6dd4-5b6c-b2ff-f734fc2a5bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366590} {:answer/id #uuid "72b528bb-8c58-5019-8054-8c8e0143306c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366591} {:answer/id #uuid "656c86e0-c53f-5510-a0dc-d24e1a0dfa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366592} {:answer/id #uuid "67b89a6b-0190-5147-bf9d-6434bf3ec618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d93c2e02-a22d-58cb-9c87-b91a9cb4dfcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366589} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b327c5c-0866-5ee8-af76-fa3afa5af268" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09857557-33a3-5971-b67f-bf80a841450b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95027" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-3{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=-3t+{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=2-3t-5{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(1-3{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(-3t+{t}^{2}) & =2-3t-5{t}^{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}t+(-3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =2-3t-5{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1.$ \n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2+1=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180fb67f-6a67-5314-a5a7-83e4f4288271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357961} {:answer/id #uuid "5273d4ec-0ed6-56c2-ad25-8714176aa52c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358460} {:answer/id #uuid "947b00dd-5c3a-5d68-97b8-f3e2c0d73d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359055} {:answer/id #uuid "a05b24ff-a2a2-55af-974a-b66d84b61f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359151} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e73b2f-7a58-5798-826f-d0fc8ea33b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a05b24ff-a2a2-55af-974a-b66d84b61f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359151} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fa47fa-89cb-527e-bbec-2ad37148ba17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d482ef0a-c05c-5115-aa27-a3051b991631" :question/math-academy-id "q-95030" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+3t-6,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2},\\,\\,q(t)=-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{t}^{2}+t-2)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}+3t-6)+{x}_{3}(-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}{t}^{3}+(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})t+(-2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-5{x}_{2}+3\\cdot 1=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=1.$"}]}
